  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-35791",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We are given the following situation for each year:\n\n- From the people who prefer basketball, $32%$ change to baseball and $28%$ change to football. This implies that $40%$ of them continue to prefer basketball.\n\n- From people who prefer baseball, $45%$ change to football and $15%$ change to basketball. This implies that $40%$ of them continue to prefer baseball.\n\n- From people who prefer football, $25%$ change to basketball and $65%$ change to baseball. This implies that $10%$ of them continue to prefer football.\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" align=\"center\">From:</td> \n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Basketball</b></td>\n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Baseball</b></td>\n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Football</b></td> \n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td rowspan=\"3\" align=\"center\">To:</td>\n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Basketball</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.15$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Baseball</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.32$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.65$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Football</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.28$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.45$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nWe can write the corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.4 & 0.15 & 0.25 \\\\ 0.32 & 0.4 & 0.65 \\\\ 0.28 & 0.45 & 0.1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.25+0.4+0.28=0.93.\n$$",
